## Notes for future research (existence checklist)

1. Triple-Alpha disambiguation is essential (identity-collision hazard):
   - **Ox Alpha** — stealth model added to OpenRouter/OpenCode 2026-08-20, 1M ctx, text/image/video in, free ~1-week preview; community rumors later resolved it as GLM-5.3-Flash (confirmed on Z.ai's own docs attribution per CN press). NOT this folder's ID.
   - **Omen Alpha** — stealth model added 2026-09-04 on OpenCode Go ($10/mo + $100 of usage), reference pricing $0.20/$0.66 (cached $0.04), commonly cited 500K context / 128K output, text+image in; OpenCode data paths point to zhipu (Zhipu AI), speculation only; tracked separately in this dataset (`model/omen-alpha/`). NOT this folder's ID.
   - **OMI Alpha** (this folder) — shares none of the above IDs or price points; the name resembles the AI-wearable product company "Omi" (BasedHardware), and the "Omen/Ox/OMI" string trio suggests a possible typo-family around the two Alpha stealth slots.
2. Search for the claimed "official OMI API" endpoint domain; confirm whether it exists at all. If the Zen catalog row's official URL or pricing link can be archived, re-evaluate.
3. If `omi-alpha` turns out to be a renamed/typo alias of `omen-alpha` (or a second serving profile of it), that identity merge/rename requires user sign-off — never self-decided.
4. Even if the slot proves real but anonymous, fingerprint/speculation evidence does not qualify as verified benchmark data (see the `exo-free` precedent — self-excluded until identity confirmation).

